About the position
Duties
Duties as a Student Guide-Interpreter include, but are not limited to:
-Communicate with visitors to Carleton Martello Tower National Historic Site in both official languages;
-Greet and provide orientation;
-Respond to visitors’ questions and complaints;
-Share information with the public about this national historic site, about other Parks Canada places in the region, or about other Saint John attractions;
-Present the history of Carleton Martello Tower to diverse audiences in an engaging way;
- Collects revenue using a Point-of-Sale system and completes daily sales reports;
- Performs light custodial tasks;
-Facilitate a safe and enjoyable visitor experience at Carleton Martello Tower by observing Compliance Guidelines;
-Contribute to a safe work environment by following safe work practices and reporting hazards;
-Assists in the organization and delivery of special events and interpretive programming.
Work environment
From its commanding position in Carleton Heights, Carleton Martello Tower has stood watch over the city of Saint John for more than two centuries. Born from the need to guard the city against a land attack from the west during the War of 1812, this Martello tower has been a witness to over 130 years of Canada’s military heritage. With one of the best lookout points in the city, visitors are rewarded with a stunning view of the Bay of Fundy, Partridge Island and the Saint John skyline. Carleton Martello Tower is looking for energetic and enthusiastic students to support our summer 2027 operations at this iconic landmark.
Student Guide-Interpreters are required to work in both the Visitor Centre and the historic tower, which consists of four floors. The grounds that surround the site are hilly and feature uneven terrain in some areas. Multiple flights of stairs provide access to the tower.
Intent of the process
The intent of this process is to hire students for the summer 2027.
